(7755368, 1282798, 140305, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the ribbon, Erin! Wow, gorgeous shot!</td>', 'Congratulations on the ribbon, Erin! Wow, gorgeous shot!', '2023-07-31 19:43:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7755374, 1282831, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by texdon:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Seriously Don 100%, absolutely fantastic photo!<br/> <br/>Adding as a favourite. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Anita, from the Queen of Silhouettes, Im just flattered by your comments. Thank you!  107 attempts. I had several with a single rider I was quite content with. I didnt even know I got this one until I downloaded the images!  Pleasantly surprised to say the least. This a full frame image, no cropping. 100 degree temps and I had to walk to the spot and didnt want to lug a second lens;  Figured Id be better off with the 70-200, wrong.  At 70 mm, my back was against a barbed wire fence with six foot dense weeds behind it.  <br/> <br/>Sunset was around 8:30 pm, and the riders had to be off the track by 8:30, so I wasnt going to get the golden light I wanted. This one was snapped at around 7. Im at the bottom of a 20 feet hill, so the illusion of sunset is there. I did have to play with this to get the light color I wanted. I actually used your latest entry as a guide. Its a natural vignette, not added. Exposure was really tricky because I could not time very well where the riders would be with the sun and they were very fast.  Ended up with a high shutter speed priority with an automatic 5 stops underexposure dialed in. Most of the riders had called it a day by 7:30 and were leaving. <br/> <br/>Thanks everyone for the wonderful comments. I know now where the higher scores come from. Wish I could figure out the 4s and 5s. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Wow, that is some backstory, thank you. You deserve the blue even more because of what you had to achieve to get this perfect shot. Usually behind every great image, theres a fantastic story, thanks for sharing. As for the lower votes, Ive worked out there are just some people that dont know a very good photo if they fell over it; and of course, then theres the other reason, which we wont go into. Its best not to think about it :)<br/> <br/>Cheers and all the best.</td>', 'Originally posted by texdon: Originally posted by Neat: Seriously Don 100%, absolutely fantastic photo! Adding as a favourite.   Anita, from the Queen of Silhouettes, Im just flattered by your comments. Thank you!  107 attempts. I had several with a single rider I was quite content with. I didnt even know I got this one until I downloaded the images!  Pleasantly surprised to say the least. This a full frame image, no cropping. 100 degree temps and I had to walk to the spot and didnt want to lug a second lens;  Figured Id be better off with the 70-200, wrong.  At 70 mm, my back was against a barbed wire fence with six foot dense weeds behind it.   Sunset was around 8:30 pm, and the riders had to be off the track by 8:30, so I wasnt going to get the golden light I wanted. This one was snapped at around 7. Im at the bottom of a 20 feet hill, so the illusion of sunset is there. I did have to play with this to get the light color I wanted. I actually used your latest entry as a guide. Its a natural vignette, not added. Exposure was really tricky because I could not time very well where the riders would be with the sun and they were very fast.  Ended up with a high shutter speed priority with an automatic 5 stops underexposure dialed in. Most of the riders had called it a day by 7:30 and were leaving.  Thanks everyone for the wonderful comments. I know now where the higher scores come from. Wish I could figure out the 4s and 5s.   Wow, that is some backstory, thank you. You deserve the blue even more because of what you had to achieve to get this perfect shot. Usually behind every great image, theres a fantastic story, thanks for sharing. As for the lower votes, Ive worked out there are just some people that dont know a very good photo if they fell over it; and of course, then theres the other reason, which we wont go into. Its best not to think about it :) Cheers and all the best.', '2023-07-31 22:03:41.000000', NULL, 0),
